Description:
    Scaffolds a new model - migration, model, policy, controller (or, for
    --nesting=tagable, a controller extension mixed into the shared
    TagablesController), views, and a full test suite - matching this app's
    own conventions rather than plain Rails scaffolding.

    Pass the model name (CamelCased, module-prefixed for a namespaced model,
    e.g. Electrical::Heater), followed by field arguments in
    name:type:option:option=value form (no spaces). See docs/GENERATORS.md
    for the full type/option reference - types include the standard Rails
    column types plus :enum, :enum_translated, and :references/:belongs_to.
    Fields can also be read from a YAML/Ruby definition file with
    --definition=name instead of listing them on the command line.

    --nesting selects the model's relationship shape: none (default),
    project, discipline, tag, document, issue, or tagable. This drives the
    model's association, its policy/controller base, and where (or whether)
    a route gets inserted.

    IMPORTANT: --nesting (and any other --option) must come AFTER every
    field argument on the command line, not before - an option placed
    earlier silently drops every field argument that follows it.

    Run with --pretend first to preview every file/edit without touching
    anything.

Examples:
    `bin/rails generate project_assistant:scaffold Electrical::Heater heater_type:enum_translated:required notes:text --nesting=tagable`
    `bin/rails generate project_assistant:scaffold DocumentControl::Issue document:references code:string --nesting=discipline`
    `bin/rails generate project_assistant:scaffold Electrical::Test --definition=electrical_test --nesting=tagable`
